Wolf's Lair: The End of Terror - test build @VERSION@

A story game made from Alexandru Georgian's novel, played on Return to
Castle Wolfenstein with a screen reader and the keyboard. It speaks
through NVDA when NVDA is running, and through the Windows voice
otherwise. This test build has the first mission: the prologue, The
Silent Shock.

You need Return to Castle Wolfenstein's own files. They are not in this
download.


INSTALL

1. Unzip this anywhere. It makes one folder.
2. Open Return to Castle Wolfenstein's own folder, then its Main folder.
   Copy these five files into the "main" folder of this download:
   pak0.pk3, sp_pak1.pk3, sp_pak2.pk3, sp_pak3.pk3, sp_pak4.pk3.
   The game will not start without sp_pak4.pk3. It may report a few
   menu errors in its console as it starts; they do no harm.
3. Run "Play the prologue". Windows may warn that the program is not
   recognised: choose More info, then Run anyway.

"Play Return to Castle Wolfenstein" starts the original game instead,
with the same speech.


STARTING

The mission screen reads the briefing. Press Enter to begin; if nothing
happens, press Enter once more, as the level finishes loading.


THE KEYS THE MODE ADDS

  H         health, armor, weapon, ammunition, and which way you face
  O         the objective, and the way to it: "the generator, ahead
            right, 12 meters"
  T (hold)  turn onto the nearest enemy in sight and stay on him;
            a tone says you are on target. Fire as usual.
  Y         every enemy in sight, nearest first
  L         the last line of the story, again
  F6        repeat the last thing said
  F8        stop speaking

The keys are added only if they are free in your configuration.


THE GAME'S OWN KEYS

  Up and Down arrows, or W and S   walk forward and back
  Left and Right arrows            turn
  A and D                          step sideways
  Ctrl                             fire
  R                                reload
  F                                use: doors, switches, the generator
  Space                            jump
  C                                crouch
  1 to 8                           weapons
  Escape                           the game menu


WHAT YOU HEAR

  A soft tone, every second and a bit, from the place you need to go
  next. Walk toward it.
  A quick tick from the nearest enemy in sight, faster the closer he is.
  A thud when you walk into a wall, from the side you hit.
  The story, as it happens. L says the last line again.


THE PROLOGUE

Revus, in the Andromeda galaxy. You break into the Great Temple of the
Ah'Zur: bring down its shield at the generator, take the Tettoran
supercolony from the sanctum past the great hall, and reach your ship on
the landing pad to the east. The sentinels of the Twelfth Legion wake
when the shield falls.


This is a test. Tell us what is hard to follow, what is said too often
or not at all, and where you got lost.

The engine is iortcw, under the GNU GPL (iortcw-COPYING.txt). The NVDA
controller client is NV Access's, under the LGPL (nvda/LICENSE.txt).
